Childhood SDoH Inputs
The second module currently exposes a dashboard subset of the broader Objective 3 trajectory program. The full Objective 3 SAP now covers five active model families: ULWOM, ULWOF, UHSES, JPA, and JMAES. The current dashboard surface does not yet display all five families. It currently uses approved preferred-scenario trajectory products for maternal co-residence (ULWOM), household socioeconomic status (UHSES), and joint maternal absence plus household socioeconomic status (JMAES). The active object is:

dashboard_sdoh_trajectories.rds

The object contains:

univariate_classes: class distributions for maternal co-residence and household SES;
joint_classes: joint maternal absence plus SES class distributions;
trajectory_profiles: estimated class-profile curves over childhood age;
class_outcomes: DPBN depression prevalence by class.

This means the dashboard guide should not be read as the full Objective 3 scope statement. It documents the current dashboard implementation subset only. The full methodological scope is defined in the integrated SAP and approved trajectory reporting bundle.

Module Acceptance Checklist
Before adding the next module, check that:

the six top-line KPI boxes are readable without clipping;
the Childhood SDoH and Mental Health window cards show both calendar window and age range;
the shared age-range slider changes all study-size, age-profile, and mediator figures and tables together;
the shared Cohort/Females/Males control changes all study-size, age-profile, and mediator cards together;
the middle overall depression prevalence updates with both the age-range slider and the analysis-stratum control;
the study-level Figure/Table switch occupies the same left-half width as Childhood SDoH + Participants + Youth Co-Creators and marks depression prevalence at the end of each study bar;
the subgroup Figure/Table switch occupies that same left-half width, keeps general cohort charts in CO-LUMINATE blue, uses distinct Frontiers-style colors for Female and Male, and marks depression prevalence above each grouped bar;
the right half beneath Mental Health + Cohorts + Depression shows all potential mediators, including HIV positive status, with paired Yes/No stacked bars, stratum-colored non-depressed distribution segments, orange depressed segments, a bottom percent axis, a top n axis, and depression-percentage markers at the bar ends;
the Childhood SDoH module shows the current dashboard subset of Objective 3 outputs: maternal co-residence, household socioeconomic status, and joint maternal absence plus household socioeconomic status class distributions, trajectory shapes, and depression prevalence by class from the approved preferred-scenario objects;
all SDoH class and outcome tables replace missing values with -, not NA;
switchable cards do not create a visible card nested inside another card;
provenance is visible enough to explain what the snapshot represents;
the page has no console errors in a browser smoke check.

